            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 12:41 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Sunday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for the Golden Horseshoe area Ontario. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: St. Catharines, Grimsby, Northern Niagara Region, Niagara Falls, Welland and Southern Niagara Region. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
